  "step_2": "The individual's verbal report is: 'Option B, weil man mit weniger Schulden aus dem Spiel geht.' This translates to: 'Option B, because one ends up with less debt from the game.' The individual is justifying the choice of B based on minimizing debt exposure. The report does not mention skewness, probabilities, or the distribution of outcomes. It focuses solely on the amount of debt incurred — specifically, that B involves a smaller loss (-3000 vs. -4000) with a lower probability (25% vs. 20%). The individual does not reference the shape of the distribution, nor does the individual mention the likelihood of avoiding loss or the concept of skewness. The deliberation process described is based on risk of loss (debt), not on the skewness of the outcome distribution.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason is about skewness — specifically, preferring a lottery with more probability mass on the favorable (non-negative) side. The individual did not consider skewness or the distributional shape. Instead, the individual justified the choice based on minimizing debt (i.e., choosing the lottery with the smaller loss), which is a different criterion (risk of loss magnitude). There is no mention of the probability of receiving 0 Euros or the asymmetry of outcomes. Therefore, the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason. The justification is based on a different reasoning principle (minimizing downside loss), not on skewness. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
